\newlabel{fig:CorchiaMC}{{\rEfLiNK{x1-3011r1}{\csname :autoref\endcsname{document}1}}{\rEfLiNK{x1-3011r1}{\csname :autoref\endcsname{document}11}}{\rEfLiNK{x1-3011r1}{\csname :autoref\endcsname{document}Output of the `Monte Carlo' algorithm for the Corchia dataset of \citet  {pollard2023}. a) Tera-Wasserburg concordia diagram with disequilibrium-corrected isochron ($t=0.5804\,\pm \,0.0086$\,Ma); b) 50 representative samples from the distribution of $^{234}$U/$^{238}$U activity ratio measurements; c) The corresponding initial $^{234}$U/$^{238}$U activity ratios; d) The isochron ages corresponding to the $[4/8]_i$ values presented in panel\leavevmode \special {t4ht@+&{35}x00A0{59}}x{}c.\vspace  \medskipamount \relax }}{document.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:AV03MC1}{{\rEfLiNK{x1-3013r2}{\csname :autoref\endcsname{document}2}}{\rEfLiNK{x1-3013r2}{\csname :autoref\endcsname{document}11}}{\rEfLiNK{x1-3013r2}{\csname :autoref\endcsname{document}Output of the `Monte Carlo' algorithm for sample AV03 of \citet  {pickering2019}. Panels\leavevmode \special {t4ht@+&{35}x00A0{59}}x{}a) -- d) are as in Figure\leavevmode \special {t4ht@+&{35}x00A0{59}}x{}\let \prOteCt \relax \let \prOteCt \relax \Protect \::ref {fig:CorchiaMC}. The black dots in panel\leavevmode \special {t4ht@+&{35}x00A0{59}}x{}b) mark synthetic replicates that are rejected because they yield physically impossible $[4/8]_i$ and/or $t$-values. The results shown in panels\leavevmode \special {t4ht@+&{35}x00A0{59}}x{}c and d are consistent with the published values.\vspace  \medskipamount \relax }}{document.1}{}}
\citation{pollard2023}
\newlabel{fig:AV03MC2}{{\rEfLiNK{x1-3015r3}{\csname :autoref\endcsname{document}3}}{\rEfLiNK{x1-3015r3}{\csname :autoref\endcsname{document}12}}{\rEfLiNK{x1-3015r3}{\csname :autoref\endcsname{document}The same data as Figure\leavevmode \special {t4ht@+&{35}x00A0{59}}x{}\let \prOteCt \relax \let \prOteCt \relax \Protect \::ref {fig:AV03MC1}, but replacing $[4/8]_m$ with the equilibrium ratio. Note that half of the synthetic replicates have been rejected (black circles). Even though there is absolutely no evidence for disequilibrium, the `Monte Carlo' produces a corrected isochron age (panel\leavevmode \special {t4ht@+&{35}x00A0{59}}x{}d) that is half the uncorrected value (panel\leavevmode \special {t4ht@+&{35}x00A0{59}}x{}a). This result is clearly wrong.\vspace  \medskipamount \relax }}{document.1}{}}
