\newlabel{fig:nomogram}{{\rEfLiNK{x1-5003r6}{\csname :autoref\endcsname{document}6}}{\rEfLiNK{x1-5003r6}{\csname :autoref\endcsname{document}16}}{\rEfLiNK{x1-5003r6}{\csname :autoref\endcsname{document} Nomogram to assess the applicability of the \textsuperscript  {206}Pb/\textsuperscript  {238}U method in the presence of different degrees of initial \textsuperscript  {234}U/\textsuperscript  {238}U-disequilibrium. Panels a and b visualise the magnitude and the precision of the disequilibrium correction, respectively, for selected values of the initial activity ratios $[4/8]_i$. $t_r$ is the uncorrected date, assuming secular equilibrium. $t_c$ is the true age, which equals the disequilibrium-corrected date using the expected $[4/8]_m$ value. $t_u$ and $t_l$ are the disequilibrium-corrected dates using present-day \textsuperscript  {234}U/\textsuperscript  {238}U activity ratios of $[4/8]_m + 2\,\unhbox \voidb@x \hbox {\a:mbox {\fontencoding  {U}\fontfamily  {wasy}\selectfont  \char 104}\b:mbox }$ and $[4/8]_m - 2\,\unhbox \voidb@x \hbox {\a:mbox {\fontencoding  {U}\fontfamily  {wasy}\selectfont  \char 104}\b:mbox }$, respectively. The dashed line in panel b) marks the relative uncertainty interval when no disequilibrium measurement is available, defined as the difference between corrected dates assuming initial ${}^{234}$U${/}^{238}$U activity ratios of 1 and 12.\relax }}{document.1}{}}
